read 16 13 "The wind altar: a basin of stone scoured smooth. Nine grooves run out from it to nine poles. The wind fills them in turn." scene=N17_ALTAR
read 15 8 "The North pole's bell: 'The wind that brings snow. Ask it for nothing; it has nothing.'"
read 21 9 "The Northeast bell: 'The wind that carries the cable. Thank it at both ends.'"
read 26 11 "The East bell: 'The sea wind. It smells of other people's harbours.'"
read 26 14 "The Southeast bell: 'The warm wind. It lies.'"
read 22 17 "The South bell: 'The wind at your back. It is not yours; it is only going your way.'"
read 14 17 "The Southwest bell: 'The wind off the salt. It keeps what it touches.'"
read 10 15 "The West bell: 'The wind that goes over the edge. It comes back as weather.'"
read 9 12 "The Northwest bell: 'The high wind. Nobody has ever heard it land.'"
read 10 9 "The ninth pole has no bell, only a groove worn in the stone. 'The wind that stopped. Listen for it.'"
read 30 12 "The cable house: the sky cable runs out over the drop toward the Shattered Choir and Crucible Isle. The winch is locked."
